diff --git a/doc/connman.conf.5.in b/doc/connman.conf.5.in
index 396f0a8..ad5eeb3 100644
--- a/doc/connman.conf.5.in
+++ b/doc/connman.conf.5.in
@@ -52,6 +52,15 @@ When BackgroundScanning is false, ConnMan will not perform any scan
 regardless of wifi is connected or not, unless it is requested by
 the user through a D-Bus call.
 .TP
+.BI WiFiMACRandomization=true\ \fR|\fB\ false
+Connect to each WiFi network with a MAC address of its own instead of
+the hardware address, and scan from random addresses. The address of a
+network is locally administered and derived from a secret kept in the
+storage directory, so it stays the same for that network across
+connections and reboots. A network can opt out through its
+UseDeviceMACAddress service property. Where the driver cannot change
+the address, the hardware address is used. Default is false.
+.TP
 .BI UseGatewaysAsTimeservers=true \fR|\fB\ false
 Assume that service gateways also function as timeservers.
 Default is false.
